{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgF8XP6b4oBQvUceBSr7z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"prompt\": \"A square, full-bleed nonrepresentational abstract painting that fills the entire canvas edge to edge, with no frame, wall, room, or gallery setting. Composition: a dense, dark indigo field at the lower half, layered with translucent veils of deep teal and ochre that thin out toward the upper right, leaving a deliberate pocket of raw unpainted cream in the upper left as empty space. Brushwork is loaded and gestural: broad, fast horizontal strokes dragged through wet paint, overlapping with tight, looping scrapes that expose underlayers of crimson and burnt sienna. Along one diagonal, a ridge of thick impasto with visible knife ridges catches light, while elsewhere the surface is scumbled and nearly matte. Contrast is strong: a few small, saturated vermilion accents sit against cool, muted greys, creating spatial tension where colors push forward and recede. Rhythm comes from repeated overlapping marks that build toward the center and then break apart at the edges. Texture varies from smooth glazed passages to rough, scraped, sanded areas. No recognizable objects, figures, faces, bodies, scenes, landscapes, horizons, machines, diagrams, symbols, icons, letters, numbers, or text. Painterly, expressive, high detail in the brushwork, even lighting with no vignette or shadowed border.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":584,"cache_read_input_tokens":15605,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":584},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"987e2c60-093d-45f8-bbc1-d459174567e2","uuid":"4e20d13e-e9e1-48f